  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 clearly outperforms pca_n2000 as RNA encoder (rna_only: 0.650 vs 0.591; multimodal+vit_l: 0.706 vs 0.635), and config_007 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) is the current best at 0.706. However, scgpt as an RNA encoder is completely untested across all 8 experiments, leaving a major gap in our understanding of the representation landscape. Question: config_030 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_007, differing only in RNA encoder. This isolates the effect of the scgpt representation while holding the best-known image encoder, aggregation, and fusion fixed. Why best next: Under limited budget, resolving where scgpt sits relative to scvi_n200 and pca_n2000 is critical—it determines whether we should invest further in scgpt-based configurations or concentrate remaining experiments on scvi_n200 variants (e.g., singleprofile, transformer aggregation). A clean A/B test here reduces uncertainty about a fundamental design axis more efficiently than testing a second-order interaction like aggregation choice, which already shows a consistent direction (avgpool > transformer)."
}

